{
  "id": "articulation-points",
  "statement": [
    "You are given an undirected graph, made of a vertex count n (vertices numbered 0 to n − 1) and a list of edges [u, v].",
    "A vertex is an articulation point (a cut vertex) when deleting it, together with its edges, splits its connected component into more pieces than before.",
    "Return all articulation points in increasing order, or none if the graph has no such vertex."
  ],
  "examples": [
